    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d629">

                <pb facs="0818" n="808" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg808"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.93/2–2747</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Secretary of the Navy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Forrestal</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-03-04">March 4, 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Thank you for your
                    letter of February 27, 1947, in regard our sending a mission to China composed
                    of men with practical knowledge in the field of government, finance, banking,
                    production, transportation and agriculture.</p>
                <p>I am in full accord with the idea and hope that conditions in China may soon make
                    it worthwhile to put it into practice. However, until we are in a position to
                    extend substantial credits to the Chinese I do not think it would be realistic
                    to send such a mission. In this connection your attention is invited to the
                    final paragraph of the enclosed <pb facs="0819" n="809" xml:id="pg809"/> copy of
                    my letter<anchor n="52" xml:id="d629-f1"/> in reply to a recent letter from
                    Secretary Patterson,<anchor n="53" xml:id="d629-f2"/> copy of which is also
                    enclosed.</p>
                <p>Sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>G. C. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
